\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Curl and the Hodge star}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{The undergraduate quotation keeps #{\operatorname{curl}}. The forms
paragraph writes the Hodge dual by right multiplication with
#{\psI^{-1}}, and the geometric paragraph writes the exterior part
#{\nabla\wedge F}. The pseudoscalar #{\psI} is named in this
discussion, and it stays distinct from the identity map #{\bbI}.}
